slos.description:
define the following terms:
a. viscous fluids,
b. non-viscous fluids;

describe the following terms:
a. fluid friction,
b. super fluidity;

define the terms:
a. specific heat,
b. molar specific heat;

compare the formation of electric field lines when:
a. same charges are brought together,
b. opposite charges are brought together;

derive a formula for equivalent resistance of two or more resistors using Kirchhoff's law in:
a. series,
b. parallel;

discuss applications of Ampere’s law in:
a. solenoid,
b. toroid;

solve word problems using the relations:
a. $E=pc$,
b. $p=\frac{hf}{c}$;

define the following terms,
a. mass defect,
b. binding energy;

explain inherent mathematical beauty in the natural world by means of:
a. elegance of simplicity,
b. symmetry;

explain the pros and cons in the debate over whether humans should research:
a. on the existence of aliens/ extraterrestrial life,
b. research into subatomic particles should continue, given the existence of nuclear weapons;
